class.description:
[VideoPresetSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"video_preset"[/code]: one call of [method apply_preset] sets the values of a [VideoPreset] in [RenderQualitySettingsServer], [TextureSettingsServer], [VideoShadowSettingsServer] and [VideoEffectSettingsServer]: all values of each domain the preset has a settings resource for ([member VideoPreset.render_quality], ...); a [code]null[/code] resource leaves its domain as it is. Changing a single value in one of these domains afterwards makes the current preset [code]"Custom"[/code] ([method get_current_preset]). The domain stores only the name of the chosen preset ([VideoPresetSettings], file [code]user://settings/video_preset.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/general/default_format] (or of its domain group [code]settings/<domain>/[/code])); the values stay in the files of the video domains. Window settings ([WindowSettingsServer]) are not part of a preset.
[b]Presets:[/b] the four built-in presets [code]"Low"[/code], [code]"Medium"[/code], [code]"High"[/code] and [code]"Ultra"[/code] ([method create_builtin_preset]) and the [code].tres[/code] files of [member ProjectSettings.settings/video_preset/presets]. A project preset with the name of a built-in preset replaces it; [member ProjectSettings.settings/video_preset/use_builtin_presets] removes the built-in presets. At runtime, [method add_preset] and [method remove_preset] change the list.
[b]One step per domain:[/b] [method apply_preset] sets all values of a domain first and applies them with one [method SettingsServer.apply] if the domain is in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE]: one [signal SettingsServer.applied] signal, one autosave and, for values with [constant SettingsServer.SETTING_FLAG_CONFIRM], one confirmation per domain. In [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_MANUAL], the values stay pending until the game calls [method SettingsServer.apply] of that domain.
[b]Renderers:[/b] values a domain doesn't support on the current renderer, hardware or build ([method SettingsServer.is_value_supported]) are skipped and keep their value; they don't count when presets are compared either. On the Compatibility renderer (default in the Web export), for example, the presets' screen-space anti-aliasing, TAA, SSAO, SSIL and SDFGI values are skipped.
[b]Custom:[/b] after a change in a video domain that is not part of [method apply_preset], the server compares the pending values with the chosen preset. If they no longer match, the first other preset that matches becomes the current one, else [code]"Custom"[/code]. A [method SettingsServer.revert] or a cancelled confirmation that restores the values gives the preset back. Domains a preset doesn't touch ([code]null[/code] resource) don't matter. Numbers are compared approximately.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	for preset_name in VideoPresetSettingsServer.get_preset_names():
		$Preset.add_item(tr(preset_name))
	VideoPresetSettingsServer.preset_changed.connect(_on_preset_changed)
	_on_preset_changed(VideoPresetSettingsServer.get_current_preset())

func _on_preset_item_selected(index):
	VideoPresetSettingsServer.apply_preset(VideoPresetSettingsServer.get_preset_names()[index])

func _on_preset_changed(preset_name):
	$CustomLabel.visible = VideoPresetSettingsServer.is_custom()
	$Preset.selected = VideoPresetSettingsServer.get_preset_names().find(preset_name)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    var presetButton = GetNode<OptionButton>("Preset");
    foreach (string presetName in VideoPresetSettingsServer.GetPresetNames())
    {
        presetButton.AddItem(Tr(presetName));
    }
    VideoPresetSettingsServer.PresetChanged += OnPresetChanged;
    OnPresetChanged(VideoPresetSettingsServer.GetCurrentPreset());
}

private void OnPresetItemSelected(long index)
{
    VideoPresetSettingsServer.ApplyPreset(VideoPresetSettingsServer.GetPresetNames()[(int)index]);
}

private void OnPresetChanged(string presetName)
{
    GetNode<Label>("CustomLabel").Visible = VideoPresetSettingsServer.IsCustom();
    GetNode<OptionButton>("Preset").Selected = System.Array.IndexOf(VideoPresetSettingsServer.GetPresetNames(), presetName);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]First start:[/b] until the player picks a preset or changes a value, the stored name is empty and [method get_current_preset] detects the preset from the values. To start with a preset that fits the hardware, apply [method suggest_preset] when the file [member SettingsServer.file_path] doesn't exist yet.
[b]Platforms:[/b] works the same on every platform; no threads, only the domain file in [code]user://[/code] and the preset files in the PCK.
